# --- Working art material (not loaded by the game) ---------------------------
# Assets/Sprites/Concepts holds generation source sheets, pilots, and
# intermediate walk-repair frames. Scripts/Tools/audit_asset_usage.py confirms
# ZERO files here are loaded at runtime; the composed atlases that actually ship
# live in Assets/Sprites/<roster>/ and are tracked normally.
#
# 563 MB of this folder is ALREADY in history as raw (non-LFS) blobs, which is
# the single largest reason .git is around 2.5 GB. These rules stop that growing.
# They cannot shrink what is already committed - that needs a history rewrite.
# The files stay on disk; they are simply not git's problem.
#
# JSON is deliberately still tracked: those provenance records are small and are
# the only surviving description of how each sheet was generated.
/Assets/Sprites/Concepts/**/*.png
/Assets/Sprites/Concepts/**/*.jpg
/Assets/Sprites/Concepts/**/*.zip
/Assets/Sprites/Concepts/**/*.import

# Same rule for the other two concept folders. Neither is referenced by any
# runtime script or scene, and together they are already 171 MB of history
# (Assets/Stages/Concepts 156.5 MB, Assets/UI/Concepts 14.9 MB per
# Scripts/Tools/audit_git_history_weight.py). They are not currently growing;
# these rules exist so a future art pass cannot silently start feeding them.
/Assets/Stages/Concepts/**/*.png
/Assets/Stages/Concepts/**/*.jpg
/Assets/Stages/Concepts/**/*.import
/Assets/UI/Concepts/**/*.png
/Assets/UI/Concepts/**/*.jpg
/Assets/UI/Concepts/**/*.import

# Superseded stage pilots. Each has a shipped successor and the asset usage
